Compose animation-core SpringSimulation.kt (Copyright 2019 The Android Open
Source Project), Apache-2.0, commit 77b2199d6f056c2fe829ce25523c34a905e769c1.
Changes: Kotlin to C#, immutable configuration, double state and seconds,
existing positive-damping validation; no Kotlin Float output rounding.
See licenses/Apache-2.0.txt.

The duration estimator (Theming/SpringDuration.cs), Oklab color conversion
(Theming/MaterialColorInterpolation.cs), system motion/shape/type tokens and
loading-indicator behavior are adapted from the same pinned AndroidX commit.
Changes: Kotlin to C#, Avalonia frame scheduling and sRGB byte-color adapter;
retained seed generation is MCU Tonal Spot Spec2021, not Android wallpaper color.

Finite tween and decay helpers (Theming/MaterialMotion.Tween.cs,
MaterialMotion.Decay.cs and MotionDecay.cs) adapt Compose tween timing,
FloatDecayAnimationSpec.kt, SplineBasedDecay.kt and FlingCalculator.kt from
the same pinned AndroidX commit (Copyright 2020 The Android Open Source
Project). Changes: C#, double state, Avalonia frame/lifecycle scheduling,
DIP density-one adapter; Android ViewConfiguration scroll friction is 0.015.

The polygon, cubic, rounding, measurement, feature matching and morph code in
Geometry/ is adapted from AndroidX graphics-shapes (Copyright 2023 The Android
Open Source Project), Apache-2.0, at the same pinned commit. Changes: C# value
types and double precision, cached MaterialShapes, Avalonia StreamGeometry paths.
Component layout, state, interaction and animation algorithms adapted from
Compose Material3 have source attribution in the register below. Native
Avalonia input, focus, automation and desktop popup adapters replace Android UI
runtime infrastructure. Custom assets and XR desktop compositions are identified
as project extensions, not official AndroidX component implementations.

